# Web builder

Script: [`scripts/build_web.py`](scripts/build_web.py). No template engine — all HTML built as Python strings.

## Do not edit generated files directly

`web/style.css` and all HTML under `web/` are regenerated by `build_web.py`. Edit the script, then re-run.

## Site navigation

Top nav: Courses · Approach · Training programme · Applied clowning · Booking · Articles · People · All other content · Content analysis.

## Key functions

| Function | Output |
|----------|--------|
| `build_index()` | `web/index.html` — courses by region, then clown level |
| `build_editorial_page()` | `web/approach.html`, `training-programme.html`, `applied-clowning.html`, `booking.html`, `articles.html` |
| `build_course_page()` | `web/courses/{slug}.html` |
| `build_people_index()` | `web/people.html` — team/associate facilitators by region |
| `build_person_page()` | `web/people/{id}.html` |
| `build_other_content_index()` | `web/other-content.html` — pages grouped by analysis category |
| `build_content_analysis_page()` | `web/content-analysis.html` |
| `build_scraped_content_page()` | `web/content/{id}.html` |
| `build_style()` | `web/style.css` |
| `markdown_to_html()` / `inline_markdown()` | Custom Markdown renderer (not CommonMark) |
| `page_shell()` | Shared HTML wrapper |

## Inputs

- Structured: `data/structured/courses.json`, `venues.json`, `people.json`
- Editorial Markdown: `data/approach.md`, `data/training-programme.md`, `data/applied-clowning.md`, `data/booking.md`, `data/articles.md` (configured in `EDITORIAL_PAGES`)
- Page analysis (optional): `data/pages_content_analysis.json`
- Raw scrape: `data/pages.json`, `articles.json`, `thoughts.json`, `testimonials.json`, `people.json`

## URL conventions

- Course slug = last segment of course `id` (e.g. `uk/events/foo-bar` → `courses/foo-bar.html`)
- Content paths mirror scrape `id` (e.g. `articles/bertilarticle` → `content/articles/bertilarticle.html`)

## Examples

- Change course list grouping → `build_index()` and helpers (`courses_by_region`, `courses_by_level`)
- Add editorial page → new `data/*.md`, entry in `EDITORIAL_PAGES`, re-run build
- Change course detail layout → `build_course_page()`

